><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14b: yes there were some practical reflections on the outcomes of the study</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="6" rect="595.276001,83.990997,779.276001,175.990997"
/></highlight
><text color="#9643FC" creationdate="D:20250709105155+10'00'" flags="print,nozoom,norotate" inreplyto="a01ae563-e126-45ce-a137-b86180c934ff" date="D:20250709105237+10'00'" name="6295468a-443a-436e-881a-2e06f4689e9f" icon="Comment" page="6" rect="305.742432,152.390366,329.742432,176.390366" subject="Sticky Note" title="Alexander Gibson"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>While&#xD;the direct observation of these mechanisms is impractical&#xD;for implementation in training environments, the analysis&#xD;of force–time data is a viable means by which practitioners&#xD;can observe the mechanical outcomes of these mechanisms.&#xD;Observing the phenomenon of synchronization can provide&#xD;insights into the strategic kinetic outcomes of simple jumping&#xD;tasks [</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.0pt;text-align:left;color:#0000FF;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>15</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>]. Further research is needed to understand the&#xD;exact relationship between this mechanical phenomenon and&#xD;the intricate SSC mechanisms. Nevertheless, practitioners&#xD;can tentatively use it as a method of determining positive and&#xD;negative kinetic strategies on the CMJ [</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.0pt;text-align:left;color:#0000FF;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>15</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>] and drop jump.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="6" rect="595.276001,84.390381,779.276001,176.390381"
/></text
></annots
